{"lines": ["In September 2026, a Cold War spy satellite broke apart in orbit, and nobody will say why.", "On September 13th, the Space Force confirmed it had fragmented, about 775 kilometres up.", "No cause. No official count of the pieces.", "It was called USA 32. A Titan II rocket lifted it from California in 1988.", "Analysts say it was Farrah III, built to listen to Soviet radar. Yes, the name matches the actress.", "Online, people asked if it was shot down on purpose. No government has said that.", "Analysts suggest something duller: an old battery or fuel tank may simply have ruptured.", "Or a tiny piece of untracked debris hit it, in one of the busiest orbits above Earth.", "One modelling firm estimates roughly 3,500 fragments bigger than a centimetre.", "Nobody has explained it. Did old hardware fail, or did something break that satellite?"], "words": [["In", 0.0, 0.1], ["September", 0.1, 0.38], ["2026,", 0.38, 1.58], ["a", 1.94, 2.08], ["Cold", 2.08, 2.3], ["War", 2.3, 2.62], ["spy", 2.62, 2.94], ["satellite", 2.94, 3.44], ["broke", 3.44, 3.8], ["apart", 3.8, 4.06], ["in", 4.06, 4.3], ["orbit,", 4.3, 4.52], ["and", 5.0, 5.1], ["nobody", 5.1, 5.32], ["will", 5.32, 5.7], ["say", 5.7, 5.94], ["why.", 5.94, 6.22], ["On", 6.88, 6.98], ["September", 6.98, 7.34], ["13th,", 7.34, 8.04], ["the", 8.56, 8.78], ["Space", 8.78, 8.96], ["Force", 8.96, 9.28], ["confirmed", 9.28, 9.74], ["it", 9.74, 10.06], ["had", 10.06, 10.18], ["fragmented,", 10.18, 10.56], ["about", 10.56, 11.38], ["775", 11.38, 12.64], ["kilometres", 12.64, 13.02], ["up.", 13.02, 13.54], ["No", 13.96, 14.08], ["cause.", 14.08, 14.36], ["No", 15.0, 15.16], ["official", 15.16, 15.44], ["count", 15.44, 15.84], ["of", 15.84, 16.02], ["the", 16.02, 16.12], ["pieces.", 16.12, 16.38], ["It", 16.94, 16.98], ["was", 16.98, 17.12], ["called", 17.12, 17.42], ["USA", 17.42, 17.86], ["32.", 17.86, 18.66], ["A", 19.22, 19.38], ["Titan", 19.38, 19.66], ["II", 19.66, 19.98], ["rocket", 19.98, 20.24], ["lifted", 20.24